{
  "id": "Lyo.Tools.Postgres",
  "name": "Lyo.Tools.Postgres",
  "area": "Tools",
  "tagline": "Spectre.Console TUI used for EF Core migrations against Lyo Postgres `DbContext`s, plus `Lyo.Seed` contributors (EF direct and Lyo.Api bulk).",
  "description": "Spectre.Console TUI used for running and rolling back EF Core migrations against Lyo Postgres `DbContext`s, plus seed contributors from `Lyo.Seed`. People can be seeded through EF or `POST Person/Bulk`; Comic is EF-only. Use it to bring a\nfresh local database up to the latest schema or step one schema back to a specific migration.",
  "features": [],
  "examples": [],
  "sections": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Startup path",
      "text": "`Program.cs` builds a default `Microsoft.Extensions.Hosting` host, wires a singleton `ConnectionStringProvider` (initial value from the `ConnectionString` config key, set in `appsettings.Development.json` or environment variables), then either runs `seed …` from argv (`SeedCli`) or hands control to `Menu.RunAsync`. Ctrl+C cancels the host. `MigrationRunner` drives EF migrations. Seed contributors (`PeopleEfSeedContributor`, `PeopleApiSeedContributor`, `ComicEfSeedContributor`) are wired through `AddLyoSeed`."
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "title": "Primary menu",
      "items": [
        "**Seeds.** Lists `Lyo.Seed` contributors (People EF, People API, Comic EF). Asks for count, optional random seed, Direct vs API when both are supported, optional skip-if-not-empty, replace for Comic, and API base URL (default `http://localhost:5251/`). CLI: `dotnet run --project Lyo.Tools.Postgres -- seed people --via ef --count 50`. `--skip` skips when rows exist; the default is append.",
        "**Migrations.** Covered below.",
        "**Change connection string.** Takes a new value and updates `ConnectionStringProvider` in place. The header shows a masked preview (`first 40 chars + ****`)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "table",
      "title": "Migration actions",
      "headers": [
        "Label",
        "DbContext",
        "Schema"
      ],
