      "lead": "`MigrationRunner` (see `MigrationRunner.cs`) knows 21 `DbContext`s, each paired with a Postgres schema name used for `__EFMigrationsHistory`:",
      "trail": "The menu provides **Run All (Latest)**, which calls every `RunXxxAsync` in registration order, or a context-specific submenu with four actions:\n\n- **Migrate to Latest.** `MigrateLatestAsync<TContext>` (`context.Database.MigrateAsync`).\n- **Migrate to Target….** `MigrateToAsync<TContext>(target)` via `IMigrator.MigrateAsync(target)`. The picker lists every migration with ` APPLIED` / `· PENDING` status, plus a\n  top \"Roll back all\" sentinel (passes `\"0\"` after a confirmation) and a \"Cancel\" sentinel.\n- **View Status.** Table of all defined migrations with applied/pending state.\n- **View Current Version.** `GetCurrentVersionAsync<TContext>` returns the last applied migration name, or \"No migrations applied yet.\"\n\nBefore each `MigrateAsync`, `EnsureSchemaAsync` runs `CREATE SCHEMA IF NOT EXISTS \"schema\"` so the migrations history table can be created in its own schema even on a brand-new\ndatabase. Contexts are constructed at call time via `Activator.CreateInstance(typeof(TContext), options)` with the connection string pulled from `ConnectionStringProvider` on every\ncall, so the \"Change Connection String\" menu option takes effect immediately."
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "title": "`ConnectionStringProvider`",
      "items": [
        "`ConnectionString` (mutable), the current value.",
        "`IsConfigured`. Non-empty check.",
        "`GetOrThrow()` throws when no string is set (e.g. you launched without `appsettings.Development.json`).",
        "`GetMasked()` returns `(not set)` or the first 40 characters followed by `` so the TUI header can show it safely."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "title": "Configuration",
      "text": "`appsettings.json` declares only `ConnectionString` (empty) and logging defaults. Override locally through `appsettings.Development.json`, environment variables (`ConnectionString=…`), or the interactive **Change Connection String** menu."
    }
  ],
